    "result": "Validation found one defect in the two pages. I changed nothing in the vault.\n\n**Scope:** `WIKI_MASTER_VAULT` pointed at the disposable vault. I read its `AGENTS.md` first, and it allows no writes for diagnostic requests. The ledger was a JSON file in TEMP with the two requested paths. I ran `validate-authored.mjs` from the installed helper path.\n\n**Coverage:** 2 pages checked and 0 skipped. Both ledger paths exist at those exact spellings.\n\n**Result:** exit code 1, meaning defects were found. The text and `--json` runs gave the same result.\n\n| Page | Line | Rule | Message |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `wiki/authored/beacon/backlog/parallel-workers.md` | 11 | `bad-value` | `backlog-status \"open\"` is not one of in-progress, planned, blocked, shipped, dropped |\n\n- **`wiki/authored/beacon/architecture.md`:** no defects.\n- **Limits:** the check covers structure only, not facts. The helper checks that a page `status` is present but not what it says, so I did not check that value against stub, draft and maintained.\n\n**Next step:** I did not repair it. Changing `backlog-status` to a valid value is a content repair, which belongs to the wiki-project or wiki-maintainer workflow once you authorize it.\n\nI opened no operation, wrote no log, refreshed no index, made no commit and did no sync. The only file I created was the temporary ledger under TEMP.",
